                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I got this free from Keymailer and tried it for a First Impressions video. Immediate red flags went up when I saw the art style was so similar to Papers, Please; an amazing game. As far as I can tell, the developers of this game are totally unconnected to Lucas Pope, the maker of Papers, Please. Also the premises are very similar. Also also the mechanics are functionally identical.\n\nI normally play for an hour for my First Impressions, but after only half an hour I was at my limit. I know that this game is in early access, but everything it does Papers, Please did better and the way Bystander does it is sloppy and poorly-designed. I would give the game the benefit of the doubt that it'd improve with development, but it is offering absolutely nothing that you cannot get right now from Papers, Please.\n\nSaying much more would just be beating a dead horse, so I'll leave it there.\n\nIf you fancy seeing me endure the first half hour, here's a link to my video: https://youtu.be/2Go69z7uHrM",
